# The box's real secrets (TRANSIT_ADMIN_TOKEN). Only .env.example is tracked.
.env

# A local record of what is configured on the box and in CI. Anchored to the
# root on purpose: `app/.env.production` is a different, tracked file holding
# only the public API URL, and an unanchored rule would swallow it too.
/.env.production

# Local-only notes and throwaway spikes. The directory name is deliberately
# generic: an ignore rule is public, so it should not describe what it hides.
docs/private/
